IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ri-works`

-- Rhode Island Works Program Rules and Regulations (218-RICR-20-00-2) -- the seat of the parent or caretaker relative who
-- applies for, or receives, RI Works cash assistance.
-- "Does my child count? Are our savings and cars within the limit? What is our standard? How much of our income counts?
-- How much will we get? How many months do I have left? What happens if I miss my employment plan? When can a cut start,
-- and does my money keep coming if I appeal?"
--
-- Every question calls the core in ri-works.l4; no rule is restated here. Each input is one fact the person can state.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `RI Works cash assistance -- the parent's or caretaker's questions`

§§ `Who counts, and resources (ss 2.5.2, 2.14)`

-- Asked once for each child.
@export Is this child an eligible child for RI Works by age (s 2.5.2)?
GIVEN `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in years
      `the child is in full-time school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a full-time student in secondary school, or at that level in a GED program or vocational or technical training
      `the child should finish by their 19th birthday month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is reasonably expected to complete that program before or in the month of their 19th birthday
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this child eligible by age` IF
    `is an eligible child by age` `the child's age` `the child is in full-time school` `the child should finish by their 19th birthday month`

@export How much of my family's property counts towards the RI Works $5,000 resource limit (s 2.14)?
GIVEN `our other countable resources` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in US dollars, less any debts against them, of your family's cash, bank accounts, stocks and bonds, real estate other than your home, and luxury items such as boats or collections (leave out your home, income-producing property and vehicles)
      `adults in our household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many adults live in your household
      `our vehicles' equity` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The equity (fair market value less what is owed) in US dollars of each vehicle your household owns that is not used mainly to produce income, listing first the ones you claim as excluded (one per adult, up to two)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our property counts` MEANS
    `the countable resources` `our other countable resources` `adults in our household` `our vehicles' equity`

@export Are my family's resources within the RI Works limit of $5,000 (s 2.14.1(A))?
GIVEN `our other countable resources` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in US dollars, less debts against them, of your family's cash, bank accounts, stocks and bonds, real estate other than your home, and luxury items (leave out your home, income-producing property and vehicles)
      `adults in our household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many adults live in your household
      `our vehicles' equity` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The equity in US dollars of each vehicle not used mainly to produce income, the ones you claim as excluded first (one per adult, up to two)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are our resources within the limit` IF
    `the resources are within the limit` (`the countable resources` `our other countable resources` `adults in our household` `our vehicles' equity`)

§§ `The standard, income and the payment (ss 2.15, 2.18)`

@export What is my family's monthly RI Works payment standard (s 2.18)?
GIVEN `people in our assistance plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How many eligible people are in your assistance plan (the eligible children and the parents or caretaker relatives included with them; leave out anyone receiving SSI)
      `we live in subsidized housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family lives in housing where the rent is restricted to a percentage of your income
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is our payment standard` MEANS
    `the payment standard` `people in our assistance plan` `we live in subsidized housing`

@export How much of my family's monthly income counts for RI Works (net adjusted income, s 2.15.5)?
GIVEN `the month` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the month you are asking about
      `first adult's gross monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gross monthly earnings in US dollars of the first adult in your assistance plan (wages, or self-employment profit); do not include your children's earnings, which are not counted
      `first adult's earnings are set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the first adult's earnings are under the earned income set aside this month (a job started while on RI Works, the household asked for the set aside, within its first six months, and household income not over 185% of the federal poverty level)
      `second adult's gross monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gross monthly earnings in US dollars of a second adult in your assistance plan (0 if none)
      `second adult's earnings are set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the second adult's earnings are under the earned income set aside this month
      `care paid for children under two` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid this month in US dollars for the care of children under two who are on RI Works
      `children under two in paid care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children under two
      `care paid for older children and incapacitated adults` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid this month in US dollars for the care of children aged two or over, or of an incapacitated adult, who are on RI Works
      `older children and incapacitated adults in paid care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children aged two or over and incapacitated adults
      `child support paid this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support paid this month by the non-custodial parent or parents, in US dollars
      `children the support is for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children the child support is paid for
      `other unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your plan's other monthly unearned income in US dollars (for example Social Security, unemployment or disability insurance, pensions, interest), leaving out EITC refunds, housing subsidies, VISTA payments and the other kinds of income s 2.15.3 excludes
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our income counts` MEANS
    `the net adjusted income`
        ((`earnings remaining after the earned income disregard` `first adult's gross monthly earnings` `first adult's earnings are set aside`)
          PLUS (`earnings remaining after the earned income disregard` `second adult's gross monthly earnings` `second adult's earnings are set aside`))
        (`the dependent care disregard` `care paid for children under two` `children under two in paid care` `care paid for older children and incapacitated adults` `older children and incapacitated adults in paid care`)
        ((`the child support counted` `the month` `child support paid this month` `children the support is for`) PLUS `other unearned income`)

@export How much RI Works cash assistance will my family get this month, if we meet the other conditions?
GIVEN `people in our assistance plan` IS A NUMBER @desc How many eligible people are in your assistance plan (leave out anyone receiving SSI)
      `we live in subsidized housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family lives in housing where the rent is restricted to a percentage of your income
      `the month` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the month you are asking about
      `first adult's gross monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gross monthly earnings in US dollars of the first adult in your assistance plan (not your children's)
      `first adult's earnings are set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the first adult's earnings are under the earned income set aside this month
      `second adult's gross monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gross monthly earnings in US dollars of a second adult in your assistance plan (0 if none)
      `second adult's earnings are set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the second adult's earnings are under the earned income set aside this month
      `care paid for children under two` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid this month in US dollars for the care of children under two who are on RI Works
      `children under two in paid care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children under two
      `care paid for older children and incapacitated adults` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid this month in US dollars for the care of children aged two or over, or of an incapacitated adult, on RI Works
      `older children and incapacitated adults in paid care` IS A NUMBER @desc How many such children aged two or over and incapacitated adults
      `child support paid this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support paid this month by the non-custodial parent or parents, in US dollars
      `children the support is for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children the child support is paid for
      `other unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your plan's other monthly unearned income in US dollars, leaving out the kinds s 2.15.3 excludes
GIVETH A `Monthly cash assistance`
`How much RI Works will we get` MEANS
    `the monthly cash assistance`
        (`What is our payment standard` `people in our assistance plan` `we live in subsidized housing`)
        (`How much of our income counts` `the month` `first adult's gross monthly earnings` `first adult's earnings are set aside` `second adult's gross monthly earnings` `second adult's earnings are set aside` `care paid for children under two` `children under two in paid care` `care paid for older children and incapacitated adults` `older children and incapacitated adults in paid care` `child support paid this month` `children the support is for` `other unearned income`)

§§ `The time limit (s 2.6)`

@export Where do I stand on the RI Works 60-month time limit (s 2.6)?
GIVEN `months of cash assistance I have had` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of family cash assistance you have received as an adult since May 1, 1997, in Rhode Island or any other state, including months under a sanction (not months as a child)
      `the children live with a parent or parents all on SSI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the children live with a single parent who receives SSI, or with two parents who both receive SSI
      `the children live with a relative caretaker not in the payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the children live with a legally responsible relative caretaker, not their parent, who is not included in the cash payment
      `DHS has granted me a hardship extension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether DHS has granted you a hardship extension beyond the time limit
GIVETH A `Time limit position`
`Where do I stand on the time limit` MEANS
    `the time limit position` `months of cash assistance I have had` `the children live with a parent or parents all on SSI` `the children live with a relative caretaker not in the payment` `DHS has granted me a hardship extension`

-- Situation: only where the person has reached, or is near, the time limit.
@export Do I meet one of the criteria for a hardship extension beyond the RI Works time limit (s 2.6.3)?
GIVEN `I have a significant incapacity and a pending SSI or SSDI claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a documented significant physical or mental incapacity, a pending SSI or SSDI application, and have applied for or are complying with an employment plan with the Office of Rehabilitation Services
      `I care full time for a disabled family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are caring for a significantly disabled family member who lives with you and needs full-time care
      `I am homeless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are homeless as the rule defines it
      `domestic violence stops me working` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a current, documented domestic violence situation makes you unable to pursue employment
      `a DHS supervisor approves another critical condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a DHS supervisor has approved another critical condition or circumstance (other than citizenship or immigration status) that makes you unable to work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet a hardship extension criterion` IF
    `meets a hardship extension criterion` `I have a significant incapacity and a pending SSI or SSDI claim` `I care full time for a disabled family member` `I am homeless` `domestic violence stops me working` `a DHS supervisor approves another critical condition`

§§ `The work penalty (s 2.11.11)`

-- Situation: only where a parent has, without good cause, not entered into or not kept to an employment plan.
@export If I do not keep to my employment plan without good cause, by how much is my family's RI Works cut each month (s 2.11.11)?
GIVEN `our family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your family's assistance plan
      `my portion as DHS works it out` IS A NUMBER @desc For a family of other than two, the portion of your family's benefit that DHS attributes to you, in US dollars (the rule does not say how it is worked out); ignored for a family of two
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is our cash cut for not keeping to my plan` MEANS
    `the work penalty reduction` `our family size` `my portion as DHS works it out`

§§ `Notice and appeal (ss 2.11.12, 2.29)`

-- Situation: only where DHS has mailed a notice that it will cut, suspend or stop the cash.
@export DHS has mailed me a notice that it will cut, suspend or stop my RI Works cash: what is the earliest day that can take effect (s 2.29.1(B))?
GIVEN `the day the notice was mailed` IS A DATE @desc The day DHS mailed the notice of adverse action
GIVETH A DATE
`When can the adverse action take effect` MEANS
    `the earliest effective date of an adverse action` `the day the notice was mailed`

@export If I ask for a hearing, does my RI Works cash keep coming until the decision (ss 2.11.12, 2.29.3)?
GIVEN `I already receive RI Works` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already receive RI Works cash (applicants do not get continued benefits)
      `days after the notice I asked for a hearing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the notice was mailed you asked for the hearing and for benefits to continue
      `the cut comes from a change in the law for everyone like me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cut is an automatic adjustment for a whole class of recipients caused by a change in State or Federal law
      `I say the grant was computed wrongly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your appeal says the grant was computed incorrectly
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my cash continue until the hearing decision` IF
    `benefits continue until the hearing decision` `I already receive RI Works` `days after the notice I asked for a hearing` `the cut comes from a change in the law for everyone like me` `I say the grant was computed wrongly`
